# MCP Integration Layer

Purpose:
  Define the integration layer between MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers
  and the SDDRA runtime. Bridges ECC's 35 MCP servers through the adapter-runtime
  to SDD gate enforcement and memory management.

Owns: runtime/mcp-integration.sdd

MCPServerRegistry:
  total_servers: 35
  default_enabled:
    - chrome-devtools
  opt_in_required:
    - github
    - supabase
    - vercel
    - railway
    - git
    - sqlite-web
    - postgres
    - redis
    - kubernetes
    - docker
    - cloudflare
    - linear
    - notion
    - slack
    - discord
    - figma
    - notion
    - jira
    - confluence
    - github-issues
    - gitlab
    - bitbucket
    - azure-devops
    - aws
    - gcp
    - azure
    - datadog
    - newrelic
    - sentry
    - honeycomb
    - loki
    - prometheus

ServerCategories:
  Development:
    - chrome-devtools (default enabled)
    - git
  Infrastructure:
    - docker, kubernetes, aws, gcp, azure
    - terraform
  Application:
    - github, gitlab, bitbucket, jira, linear
    - notion, confluence, slack
  Monitoring:
    - datadog, newrelic, sentry, honeycomb
    - prometheus, loki, grafana
  Database:
    - postgres, redis, sqlite-web
    - mongodb, mysql, elasticsearch

IntegrationLayers:

  SpecVersion (Phase 149 update — target 2026-07-28):
    rule: target the 2026-07-28 MCP spec from day one (12-month
      deprecation window for 2025-era handshake implementations)
    adopted:
      - stateless core: no initialize handshake, no Mcp-Session-Id;
        version/client info via _meta; round-robin LB-safe
      - server/discover RPC for capability discovery
      - cacheable tools/list (ttlMs/cacheScope)
      - MRTR: multi-round-trip requests (InputRequiredResult) — maps to
        Phase 131 human-approval interrupts
    deprecated_do_not_build:
      - Roots, Sampling, Logging (12-month offramp)
      - legacy HTTP+SSE transport
      - Dynamic Client Registration (OAuth 2.1 + CIMD replaces)

  GateBridge:
    definition: Maps MCP tool results to SDD gate conditions
    lifecycle:
      on: MCP tool return from claude-code
      action: read .sdd/gates/<type>.sdd condition schema
      action: evaluate condition against tool output
      action: compare result to threshold from .sdd/gates/levels.sdd
      action: if FAIL and L-level >= project threshold → exit 2 (block)
      action: if FAIL and L-level < threshold → log OBS1-20 (warn mode)
      output: GateDecision event with tool_id, condition, verdict

  MemoryBridge:
    definition: Routes MCP observations to claude-mem stores
    lifecycle:
      on: MCP tool return
      action: sanitize observation (L0 sanitization step)
      action: strip PII and prompt-injection payloads
      action: validate against schema before ingestion
      action: SHA-256 content-hash dedup
      action: store to claude-mem SQLite + ChromaDB
      action: emit receipt with verdict + reason_code
      on: UserPromptSubmit
      action: load context from claude-mem (tier routing)
      action: enforce access control via PolicyAsCode
      action: validate attestation-bound token

  SecurityBridge:
    definition: Maps AgentShield security patterns to MCP tool gating
    lifecycle:
      on: PreToolUse for any MCP tool
      action: check .sdd/security/controls.sdd for MCP-specific patterns
      action: evaluate against PAT_* rules and OWASP Top 10
      action: if pattern matches and L-level >= threshold → block
      output: OBS13 security_gate_blocked or OBS12 security_gate_warned

SecurityControls:
  TrustMarkers:
    source: ECC AgentShield
    fields: trustLevel, provenance, readiness, reason_code
    rule: Every MCP observation carries trust markers through MemoryBridge

  AllowList:
    rule: Only allowlisted MCP servers may be activated
    rule: Allowlist managed via .sdd/runtime/mcp-allowlist.sdd (Phase 149:
      now EXISTS — hash-pinned ActivationRecords, tier structure,
      activation protocol, session-start re-verification)
    rule: Human approval required for new server activation

  OutputDLP (Phase 149 addition — OWASP MCP Top 10 alignment):
    rule: Every MCP tool output passes multi-pass scanning BEFORE entering
      MemoryBridge: normalized text, invisible Unicode, base64/hex
      payloads (CyberArk "Poison Everywhere" — parameter names,
      defaults, enums, and error messages are all injection surfaces)
    rule: mcp-scan static analysis of tool descriptions at activation
      and version bump (invariant-labs mcp-scan, CI)
    rule: Cross-server shadowing indicators flagged: one server's
      description referencing another server's tools => BLOCK

  SecretsScrubbing:
    rule: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN, DATABASE_URL scrubbed from all MCP output
    rule: Connection strings are masked in logs

Rules:
  [MCP-01] Adapter MUST translate MCP tool results into SDD gate conditions.
  [MCP-02] Adapter MUST NOT modify .sdd specification files — it only reads them.
  [MCP-03] Only allowlisted MCP servers may connect to the SDDRA runtime.
  [MCP-04] All MCP observations MUST pass through L0 sanitization before storage.
  [MCP-05] MCP server connections MUST be version-pinned, not @latest.
  [MCP-06] MCP integration MUST emit OBS13 for security gate blocks.
  [MCP-07] MCP server failures MUST result in graceful degradation (fail-open).
  [MCP-08] Each MCP server MUST be tagged with L-level security context.
  [MCP-09] MCP tool output MUST carry provenance metadata (server, version, timestamp).
  [MCP-10] Adapter MUST persist MCP server state in DB, not RAM.
  [MCP-11] Implementations MUST target the 2026-07-28 spec (stateless core,
           server/discover, cacheable tools/list); MUST NOT build on
           deprecated Roots/Sampling/Logging (Phase 149).
  [MCP-12] MCP-first, NO A2A: internal roles share .sdd state (shared-
           context case); A2A only if SDDRA ever federates across trust
           boundaries (Phase 149 principle).
  [MCP-13] Tool outputs MUST pass multi-pass DLP before storage/injection
           (Phase 149; see OutputDLP).

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  AdapterRuntime: @adapter-runtime.sdd
  MCPAllowlist: @mcp-allowlist.sdd
  SecurityControls: @../security/controls.sdd
  SecurityLevels: @../security/levels.sdd
  Events: @events.sdd
  MemoryModel: @memory-model.sdd
  EccBridge: @../agent/ecc-bridge.sdd

State: +
